        # rule 1 clause 2's licence for a later placement is a NAMED invalidator, and this check has
        # one — another session can dirty main DURING the minutes-long verify, which only the in-lock
        # call can catch. Deleting either of them because "the early arm covers it" is the specific
        # failure this placement is written against.
        #
        # FIRES ON A SOLO LAND. This sits on `cmd_land`'s unconditional straight line, above any batch
        # formation; a branch landing ALONE executes it identically. The saving is not "protect the
        # queued neighbours" — it is "stop paying the expensive stage to learn something cheap".
