# ── T-11463 (SPEC-0181) — the verifier fence by REACHABILITY, not by path and NEVER by NAME ──────
# `bin/**` refuses a land's selection wholesale, and 53.6% of blocking commits since 2026-08-01 are
# inside ONE file (bin/lib/worktree.py, 327 top-level defs) whose most-edited functions are
# land-integration bookkeeping that cannot influence WHICH TESTS ARE SELECTED. Narrowing the glob by
# FILE recovers ~1.3%; the recoverable share is INSIDE the file. So the question changes from "did the
# diff touch bin/**" to "did the diff touch code that PARTICIPATES IN THE SELECTION DECISION".
#
# PARTICIPATION IS REACHABILITY OVER THE CALL GRAPH — a name matcher is wrong in BOTH directions and
# the codebase carries both counter-examples: `_land_integrate` names nothing about verify yet
# composes the decision's inputs and opts the land into governing, while `_verify_failure_excerpt`
# names verify yet only formats an error string. Roots are SPEC-0181's own `implements:` set plus the
# fence carriers it delegates to; PARTICIPATING = the roots' DESCENDANTS (what the decision EXECUTES)
# ∪ their ANCESTORS (what FEEDS or INVOKES it). Either direction alone frees one of those two.
_SELECTION_DECISION_ROOTS = (
    "_shadow_select",                       # SPEC-0181 implements: the decision itself
    "_selection_governs",                   # SPEC-0181 implements: may this land ACT on it
    "_selection_recorded_misses",           # SPEC-0181 implements: the governing window
    "_selection_omission_tripwire",         # SPEC-0181 implements: the omission oracle
    "_selection_coverage_map",              # the map the decision reads
    "_verify_skip_fail_closed_edge",        # the shared fail-closed rungs it delegates to
    "_verify_implementation_touch_globs",   # the ONE matching carrier (T-11460)
    "_is_verify_implementation_touch",      # its bool()
    "_selection_leaf_test_freed",           # the T-11461 narrowing it applies
    # T-11521 (SPEC-0181 R1) — THE CLASSIFIERS THAT DECIDE WHAT IS FREED FROM THIS RUNG ARE THEMSELVES
    # ROOTS. This completes the construction the comment above already declares ("plus the fence
    # carriers it delegates to") rather than adding a rule: T-11463 duly rooted its OWN classifier
    # `_selection_leaf_test_freed` one line up, but T-11511's SIBLING classifier was never rooted, and
    # neither were the three pure helpers the reachability prover delegates to.
    # MEASURED on main before this change: NONE of the five was in the participating set, so a land
    # whose diff touched only `_selection_periphery_freed` was FREED from R1 BY THE VERY RULE IT WAS
    # EDITING and earned an omission — while SPEC-0181 states the opposite guarantee ("weakening the
    # EXECUTABLE rule therefore requires editing code under the verifier surface, which rung R1 already
    # forces to the full suite"). That is the asymmetry
    # lessons/carving-an-exception-into-a-fail-closed-gate §1 names: an exception's discriminator must
    # not be able to relax itself unobserved.
    # DIRECTION: this WIDENS refusal (participating 24 → 29 of 368 top-level defs). It cannot narrow
    # anything and cannot reach the SPEC-0077 pinned leg, which passes `reachability_freed=None`.
    "_selection_periphery_freed",           # T-11511's allowlist classifier — the freed set it asserts
    "_selection_reachability_freed",        # T-11463's prover — the freed set it proves
    "_selection_participating_defs",        # the participation reasoning the prover delegates to
    "_selection_changed_def_owners",        # …and the attribution it fails closed on
    "_selection_diff_hunk_ranges",          # …and the hunk parse it fails closed on
    # T-12005 — the CROSS-MODULE reachability read `_selection_decision_reaches_root_handlers` (the
    # discriminator that tells a read-only REPLAY of a root from a PARTICIPANT, and so decides what
    # limb B of the T-11654 membership test frees) belongs to this family and is DELIBERATELY NOT
    # LISTED HERE — the same call for the same reason as `_selection_host_injected_roots` just above.
    # It CITES that function, which is itself an ancestor of the root `_selection_participating_defs`,
    # so the ancestor half of the closure already makes it participate; MEASURED on this tree, not
    # assumed — with the name absent from this tuple it is still in
    # `_selection_participating_defs(worktree.py)`, and it drops OUT the moment the five classifiers
    # above are un-rooted, which is the control that proves the coverage flows from these roots rather
    # than from an incidental edge (the arm is in tests/test_t11511_bin_periphery_allowlist.py §AC4).
    # Listing it would be a redundant entity, not a stronger guard, and would DISARM that control by
    # making it participate for a second, unrelated reason.
    # T-11876 — the cross-module root derivation `_selection_host_injected_roots` belongs to this
    # family (it decides what may be freed from a non-host module, so editing it must not be freed by
    # the very rule it edits, per the T-11521 construction above) — and it is DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED
    # HERE, because listing it would be a redundant entity, not a stronger guard. It is CALLED by
    # `_selection_reachability_freed`, which IS a root, so the DESCENDANT half of the closure already
    # makes it participate; MEASURED, not assumed — with the name absent from this tuple it is still
    # in `_selection_participating_defs(worktree.py)`. Listing it would also silently DISARM the AC1c
    # differential in tests/test_verify_implementation_rule_narrowed.py, which un-roots the five
    # classifiers and requires each to go back to being freed: a sixth root reaching two of them keeps
    # them participating and the differential stops discriminating. The guard is kept BY THE CALL EDGE.
)

# The files this fence reasons INSIDE. Deliberately not "every bin/ python file": every other verifier
# path keeps refusing on the glob exactly as before.
#
# T-11876 WIDENED THIS FROM ONE FILE TO THREE, and the tuple was never the blocker — the PROVER was.
# `_selection_participating_defs` returns None unless the module DEFINES every `_SELECTION_DECISION_ROOTS`
# name, which no EXTRACTED module does, so merely naming batch_landing.py here would have freed exactly
# nothing while looking like it did something. What the two additions need is the CROSS-MODULE edge: the
# host does not call these modules' defs by the root names, it binds them back as residues and by keyword
# (`_land_batch_verify_path_touch` -> the host's `_verify_path_touch`), so a module's real roots are its
# own defs CITED INSIDE THE HOST'S PARTICIPATING DEFS — derived by `_selection_host_injected_roots`.
#
# WHY THESE TWO AND NOT THE OTHER EXTRACTED MODULES: they are precisely the two the T-11654 membership
# test REFUSES for the `bin/**` periphery allowlist (batch_landing.py gates a verify leg; both are
# read by the land path), i.e. the two that must keep being reasoned about rather than freed wholesale.
# A module already ON that allowlist needs nothing here. MEASURED on this tree at the time of the
# change: batch_landing.py 54 injected roots -> 1 of 95 defs (1.1%) freeable; rebaseline_currency.py
# 30 injected roots -> 4 of 56 defs (7.1%) freeable. Small, and quoted as measured rather than as the
# card's commit-level 6.53pp, which is a different denominator.
_SELECTION_REACHABILITY_FILES = (
    "bin/lib/worktree.py",              # the HOST — reasoned about with the roots defined IN it
    "bin/lib/batch_landing.py",         # T-11876 — cross-module, roots derived from the host's citations
    "bin/lib/rebaseline_currency.py",   # T-11876 — likewise
)
_SELECTION_REACHABILITY_HOST = "bin/lib/worktree.py"

# T-12005 — the modules the selection DECISION ITSELF lives in. Distinct from
# `_SELECTION_REACHABILITY_FILES` above, which names the modules the fence reasons INSIDE (its two
# non-host members are subjects of the fence, not homes of the decision). These two are where the
