# a reader to raise: its fold rewrites `events.jsonl`, which `_selection_recorded_misses` reads — but
# that exposure is SHARED with the already-audited `events.py` / `journal.py` members, so it is not a
# discriminator between them, and it is not the membership test this list is governed by.
#
# THE ONE ENTRY T-11522 ADDED, and it is the membership test above applied rather than an exception
# to it: `bin/lib/worktree_lifecycle.py` — the worktree-LIFECYCLE verbs (`worktree new` / `adopt` /
# `park` / `sweep` / `sync` / `recover-land`) and their exclusive mechanism, extracted from
