# ── T-11216 — the eviction probe's stage source: `merge-tree --write-tree -z` conflicted-file info ──
# A `git merge --no-edit main` leaves its three conflict stages in the INDEX, which is what
# `_classify_land_merge_conflicts`'s resolvers read. The rule-3 probe has no index and may not
# acquire one — it must judge without checking anything out. It does not need to: `merge-tree
# --write-tree` ALREADY prints those exact stages. Under `-z` the stream is NUL-separated fields —
# the merged tree oid, then `<mode> <oid> <stage>\t<path>` records, then an EMPTY field closing the
# section, then informational messages. `-z` (rather than line parsing) because the terminator is
# unambiguous and a path can carry anything but NUL. Verified against git 2.43.0.
# The probe outcomes that mean "this member merges" — a merge git resolved by itself, and one the
# land path's own classifier resolves. Named rather than spelled twice: the head accumulator and the
# peer loop must NEVER disagree about what merging means, and a set they both read is the only shape
# where that cannot drift. `conflict` / `unevaluable` are deliberately absent (T-11216).
_LAND_PROBE_MERGEABLE = batch_landing._LAND_PROBE_MERGEABLE  # T-11524 host re-export alias — moved WITH its readers


