# ── T-11335 (SPEC-0184 rule 4) — the RED-BATCH ISOLATION ORACLE ───────────────────────────────────
# THE ASYMMETRY THIS CLOSES. A member that cannot MERGE is evicted and the rest carry on
# (`evicted-for-conflict`, rule 3). A member that fails the TESTS turns the whole batch red and EVERY
# peer is requeued, including provably unrelated ones. Same batch, two failure modes, opposite blast
# radius — and measured over the whole journal the requeue is the LARGEST non-landing category: 39
# member-slots against 20 evicted-for-conflict. The 2026-08-19T20:07:40Z batch landed NOBODY and
# requeued three; `task/T-11326` (a graph-build cache) was unrelated to all three failing assertions
# and paid ~19 minutes of pure overhead inside a 45-minute land.
#
# WHY T-11259'S ATTRIBUTION COULD NOT CLOSE IT, AND IS NOT WIDENED HERE. That function attributes by
# "exactly one member MODIFIED that test's path" (its gate 4), which catches «I changed behaviour and
# my own pinned test is now superseded» and is correctly SILENT on the more damaging case: a member
# whose CODE breaks a test it never edited. Widening gate 4 to guess at that would manufacture the
# plausible-wrong answer its whole shape refuses. So the answer is not a wider heuristic, it is an
# ORACLE: re-run ONLY the FAILING assertions against each member ALONE and read what actually
# happens. Cheap by construction — the failing set is typically one to three files and the batch is
# at most `_LAND_BATCH_MAX`; it is not a suite pass per member. T-11259's report-only marks are
# untouched by this file (and never collide: gate 1 below refuses the pinned entries they read).
#
# THE THREE OUTCOMES, AND THE THIRD IS NOT OPTIONAL (named by the external-auditor consult
# `decisions/batch-member-rebaseline-authority-audit-adhoc.yaml`, 2026-08-19): exactly one member
# fails alone -> evict it and carry the rest; several fail alone -> evict each; NO member fails alone
# -> the failure is an INTERACTION of the merged tree, nobody may be evicted, and today's
# requeue-everyone is the correct answer rather than a misattribution to whichever member a search
# happened to isolate first. That consult also fixes this function's ROLE: "keep the merged-tree
# pinned leg as the protective check; use per-member or subset runs only as DIAGNOSTICS for
# attribution". Nothing here is a gate — it decides nothing and gates nothing; the caller acts.
_LAND_RED_ISOLATION_OUTCOMES = ("culprits", "interaction", "partially-explained", "undecidable")

# `_run_verify_tests` reports a subprocess it could not even START in the SAME
# `"test failed: <name>\n<tail>"` shape as a real assertion failure. Reading that as "this member
# reproduced the failure" is exactly the bypass `lessons/carving-an-exception-into-a-fail-closed-gate`
# §1 describes: the runner's OWN error would nominate an innocent branch as the culprit. So the
# marker is matched explicitly and turns the WHOLE probe undecidable.
