# ───────── T-11479 (SPEC-0077 §3a × T-10850) — WAIVE COVERAGE JUDGED AT THE STEP-4A PREFLIGHT ─────────
#
# MEASURED. `--rebaseline-unauthorized` carries TWO refusal arms and only one had been moved off the
# expensive path. T-10850 moved the [authorization] arm (`_change_is_audited`) to the step-4a preflight;
# the [waive-coverage] arm still reads `pinned_bad` and so is raised only AFTER the SPEC-0132 admission
# slot and the FULL pinned run — 22 aborts / 323.4 min in the 7 days to 2026-08-23 (the SPEC-0119 debt
# echo, which reports the two arms separately for exactly this reason, T-11426). The one pre-verify
# judgement that exists, `_rebaseline_admits_past_backstop`, is gated on `ra_count >=
# LAND_REPEATED_ABORT_THRESHOLD` and judges only assertions PRIOR aborts recorded — so a FIRST land, and
# any branch whose named check has never failed on record, gets no pre-verify judgement at all. That
# NO-RECORDS case is the residual none of T-11242 / T-11257 / T-11347 / T-11375 reaches: each of those
# needs recorded failing assertions to work from.
#
# HYPOTHESIS, NOT A REALISED SAVING. What is proven here is the MECHANISM — a token that cannot bind is
# refused BEFORE the pinned run. How much of the measured 323.4 min this recovers is NOT claimed: the
# echo does not separate first-land from repeat-land, and the honest probe is that the refusal moves
# earlier, not that a week of minutes is already back (the card's own framing, kept).
#
# ONE JUDGING AUTHORITY, NOT TWO. The verdict comes from `_rebaseline_waive_coverage` — the SAME call
# the grant makes, classifier and judge both. No second matcher is introduced, which is precisely the
# drift T-11002 factored `_waive_coverage_over_records` out to prevent (CHARTER §P5).
#
# IT REFUSES ON `bad_tokens` ONLY, NEVER ON `uncovered` — and that bound is the whole reason this is
# not a strictness delta. A token is judged against the pinned outcome of the very file IT NAMES, and
# that outcome is authoritative: `_run_verify_tests` executes each file as its OWN subprocess against
# its OWN tempfile.mkdtemp git repo, so a per-file verdict does not move when the suite runs beside it.
# Suite-WIDE coverage is a different fact, owned only by the full run — `uncovered` is therefore
# discarded here and left to the grant. What this refuses is a strict SUBSET of what the grant already
# refuses; it never refuses something the grant would admit.
#
# FAIL-OPEN ON EVERY UNPROVEN INPUT. No declaration, no key resolving to a last-green test file, a
# pinned setup/driver failure, an unreadable result — every one of them ADMITS the land and falls
# through to today's behaviour. A guard whose job is to make a refusal CHEAPER must never be able to
# invent one; the expensive refusal downstream is unchanged and still authoritative.
#
# NO NEW VOCABULARY. The EXISTING `rebaseline-unauthorized` class and the EXISTING `abort_preflight`
# row shape (T-10850) — which is also what keeps this cheap refusal exempt from the T-0655 streak. No
# new store, no new gate, no new abort class, no placement enum.

# Entries a pinned run returns that are NOT a check verdict but a statement about the CHECKER. Any of
# them makes the acquisition inconclusive, which ADMITS (see fail-open above).
_PREFLIGHT_ACQUIRE_INCONCLUSIVE = ("setup FAILED", "pinned-engine subprocess FAILED",
                                   "pinned-engine subprocess produced no result file",
                                   "pinned-engine result unreadable")


